1506096.steps:
1. Configure X0 as default LAN using a static IP, configure X1 as primary WAN using static IP, configure X2 as secondary WAN using DHCP mode;
2. Enable Load Balancing, select spill-over based WLB, configure that send traffic to Secondary WAN when bandwidth exceeds 10 kbps;<span class="Apple-converted-space"> 3. Set the src-dst checkbox to the ON setting to enable source and destination IP address binding;
4. Send high volume traffic with high diversity of destinations , with different service, e.g. FTP,HTTPS, HTTP, PING, observe the packet monitor, find out which WAN interface that each traffic go through;
5. Verify that same source-destination pairs are persistent to the same interface;
6. Reboot DUT;
7. Verify that same source-destination pairs are still persistent to the same interface;

