1506092.steps:
1. Configure X0 as default LAN using a static IP, configure X1 as primary WAN using static IP, configure X2 as secondary WAN using DHCP mode; 2. Enable Load Balancing Method with Spill-over Based; 3. Start with src-dst checkbox in OFF setting;
4. Configure that send traffic to Secondary WAN when bandwidth exceeds 10 kbps. 5. Start traffic from same source IP address and same destination IP address, but with different source TCP ports and different destination TCP ports e.g. FTP traffic, HTTP traffic from source 192.168.168.1 to destination 10.0.200.2. and make sure one of them exceeds 10 kbps, Spill-over should happen.
6. Set the src-dst checkbox to the ON setting to enable source and destination IP address binding ;
7. Start FTP traffic from 192.168.168.2 to destination 10.0.200.3, download a large file to make sure this traffic exceeds 10kbps, and then start another Ping traffic, from 192.168.168.2 to destination 10.0.200.3;
8. Observe all the traffic in packet monitor, all traffic must only go to one particular WAN interface depending on which one has less load.

